From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 08:51:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Add _LPI hierarchy
 extraction callback

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

ACPI processor _LPI parsing already walks processor-container ancestors to
build the flattened cpuidle state table. Hierarchical domain construction
needs to inspect each raw firmware level without duplicating that parser.

Add an ACPI-internal extraction callback that reports each raw level before
flattening. Level 0 is the processor leaf and each processor-container
ancestor increments the level. The callback-owned state view is valid only
while the callback runs. Keep its declaration private to ACPI, but
namespace-export the implementation for the processor module. Retain the
existing exported extraction interface for other users.

Validate the _LPI state-count object before reading its integer value.
Record and validate the LevelId in every parsed state so callback consumers
can distinguish otherwise identical domain descriptions. Move the common
composition helper to the processor header so both the legacy flattening
path and hierarchy consumers use the same algorithm.

A missing parent _LPI method terminates the hierarchy normally. Preserve
the legacy handling of a parent evaluation failure, while callback
consumers receive the error so they cannot accept a partial hierarchy.
Route failures through one allocation cleanup path.

